Subject: [PATCH 15/15] startup: exit non-zero when a migrate or seed run fails

Intent: StartServer catches every exception, logs "Error while starting
server" and returns, and Main only sets a non-zero exit code for bad
arguments or a missing web client directory. In --mode MigrateSystem or
SeedSystem a failing CoreInitialisation or AppInitialisation migration
is therefore restored from the pre-migration dump and the process still
exits 0, so a Kubernetes migration Job reports Succeeded after a failed
and rolled-back pass. In those two modes the catch now sets
Environment.ExitCode = 1; the server mode is unchanged. A failure in
PreInitialisation already escapes StartApp and exits non-zero.
Proven with the image: --mode MigrateSystem against an unreachable
PostgreSQL exits 1, a successful pass exits 0; the smoke asserts the
migrate container exits 0 and never logs "Error while starting server".
Drop when: upstream exits non-zero on a failed one-shot startup mode.

Patch: 0023
---
 Jellyfin.Server/Program.cs | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Jellyfin.Server/Program.cs b/Jellyfin.Server/Program.cs
index 50fc05d..d558b93 100644
--- a/Jellyfin.Server/Program.cs
+++ b/Jellyfin.Server/Program.cs
@@ -256,6 +256,12 @@ namespace Jellyfin.Server
             {
                 _restartOnShutdown = false;
                 _logger.LogCritical(ex, "Error while starting server");
+
+                // A one-shot run (a migration Job) must report its failure; the server mode keeps upstream's exit.
+                if (options.StartupMode is Configuration.StartupMode.MigrateSystem or Configuration.StartupMode.SeedSystem)
+                {
+                    Environment.ExitCode = 1;
+                }
                 if (_setupServer!.IsAlive && !configurationCompleted)
                 {
                     _setupServer!.SoftStop();
